  "question": {
    "text": "Two point charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;each are placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math> apart. A third point charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> is placed at a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> from mid-point on the perpendicular bisector. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;at which charge <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math> will experience the maximum Coulomb&#39;s force is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "vSxP8",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MvECU",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uESDd",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mlBUE",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/25284b10-22d6-400c-9e5e-424dbd9ad6ad-image.png\" style=\"width: 230px; height: 240px;\" /></p><p>The distance between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math>.</p><p>The force between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>.</p><p>From the given figure we can see that only vertical components of the forces will add, and the&nbsp;horizontal components will get cancelled out.&nbsp;Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi></mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>For force to be maximum,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>d</mo><msub><mi>F</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mi>q</mi><mi>Q</mi><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><msup><mfenced><msup><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p>",
